        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-2$: single root; $x=3$: double root.",
          "worked": "The factor $(x+2)$ has exponent $1$, so $x=-2$ is a single root. The factor $(x-3)^2$ has exponent $2$, so $x=3$ is a double root.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=(x+1)(x-3)(x+5)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1,3,-5$: all single roots.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}x+1&=0 &&\\text{gives }x=-1\\\\x-3&=0 &&\\text{gives }x=3\\\\x+5&=0 &&\\text{gives }x=-5\\end{aligned}$\n\nEach linear factor has exponent $1$, so all three roots are single.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=(x-5)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=5$: double root.",
          "worked": "$x-5=0$ gives $x=5$. The factor has exponent $2$, so this is a double root.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=(x+4)^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-4$: triple root.",
          "worked": "$x+4=0$ gives $x=-4$. The factor has exponent $3$, so this is a triple root.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=(x-2)^2(x+4)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$: double root; $x=-4$: single root.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}x-2&=0 &&\\text{gives }x=2\\\\x+4&=0 &&\\text{gives }x=-4\\end{aligned}$\n\nThe respective factor exponents are $2$ and $1$, so the roots are double and single.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=(x+7)^3(x+3)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-7$: triple root; $x=-3$: single root.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}x+7&=0 &&\\text{gives }x=-7\\\\x+3&=0 &&\\text{gives }x=-3\\end{aligned}$\n\nThe respective factor exponents are $3$ and $1$, so the roots are triple and single.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=(x+7)^3(x+3)^2(x-1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-7$: triple root; $x=-3$: double root; $x=1$: single root.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{aligned}x+7&=0 &&\\text{gives }x=-7\\\\x+3&=0 &&\\text{gives }x=-3\\\\x-1&=0 &&\\text{gives }x=1\\end{aligned}$\n\nThe respective factor exponents are $3$, $2$ and $1$, so the roots are triple, double and single.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
