        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,-1$: both double roots.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=((x-1)(x+1))^2\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)^2(x+1)^2\\end{align*}$\n\nThe roots are $x=1$ and $x=-1$. Both linear factors have exponent $2$, so both roots are double.",
